cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bayesSampleMix: Contamination-Aware Bayesian Integration of Probability and Non-Probability Samples"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dapr12/bayesSampleMix"
url: "https://github.com/dapr12/bayesSampleMix"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian contamination-mixture regression for combining a trusted
  probability sample with a non-probability sample that may contain units
  incompatible with the target model. Each non-probability unit carries a
  latent compatibility indicator sampled by data augmentation, yielding
  posterior inference for regression coefficients, the contamination
  fraction and unit-level filter scores. Gaussian, logistic (Polya-Gamma)
  and Poisson regressions are supported.
keywords:
  - R
  - Bayesian inference
  - data integration
  - non-probability samples
  - survey statistics
  - mixture models
  - MCMC
authors:
